WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.200
Missing audit logs leave teams unable to reconstruct important events.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.980
Applications should capture authentication activity, authorization failures,

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.680
administrative actions, sensitive data access, configuration changes,

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.900
and high-risk workflow events.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:20.280
Poor alerting creates noise without action or misses the events that matter most.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.340
Alerts should focus on anomalies, suspicious access, high-risk changes,

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.800
and activity affecting sensitive data.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:30.540
Delayed incident detection increases attacker dwell time and impact.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.760
Without monitoring and review, compromise, insider abuse,

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.260
and data access anomalies may continue unnoticed.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.520
Incomplete monitoring can also weaken SOC 2 readiness.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.060
Logs need retention, integrity, ownership, review procedures,

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.480
and escalation paths that support investigation and evidence.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.500
Centralize logging from applications, identity systems, infrastructure,

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.200
and cloud services. Integrate telemetry with SIEM or monitoring workflows.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:03.260
Create security alerting and review processes for high-risk events.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:09.800
Selected SOC 2 mappings for this topic include CC7.2 - Monitoring activities;

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:13.700
CC7.3 - Incident detection and response support.
